  {
    "sha": "bf752be65aa056f14b05df1e79729d5a9eac3b00",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGJmNzUyYmU2NWFhMDU2ZjE0YjA1ZGYxZTc5NzI5ZDVhOWVhYzNiMDA",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-15T18:23:27Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-15T18:23:27Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(test): hold the bore's Adaptive pin to the part silhouette after #1774\n\nThe release gate of the 0.21.0 cut (run 43739171721) failed\npocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean\nat its #850 assert (no planning budget). The notes said that the HSM plan\nran past its growth budget at Z 15 and Z 5, would post 124740 moves at\nZ 10, and left 22% uncut at Z 0 - Offset rings cut those levels instead.\nThe worst corner scallop stood at (34.99, -34.99): the stock corner, far\noutside the 60 mm disc. Windows fails the same way (605.2 k vertices), so\nthe failure does not depend on the OS.\n\nCause: PR #1780 (#1774) makes a whole-model 3D Pocket clear the stock\naround the model out to the stock outline. That is intended and reviewed.\nWith the 70 x 70 block the level is now one wide ring with the part as\nits island, not the bore that this test pins. The fallbacks are named in\nthe notes and the path verifies clean, so the product is not wrong.\n\nThe test now sets Tool containment: Inside on the op (one\nEditOperationParams::with_area command). For the pocket family that is\nthe native containment, so boundary::resolve gives back the source-built\nsilhouette unchanged, and a controlled region skips the open-side growth.\nThe footprint is then the one the test always pinned. No assert changed.\nReading on Windows x86_64, release: (16017, 15360, 1427), the exact\n#1402 triple, with no budget note and no fallback.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
